I can give you the node, but not with the change as described.

The node's authority is its `with` clause, and that clause grants exactly `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0` — a model-access interface with no tool calling and no outbound I/O. The requested change is to add an HTTP `GET` to `https://metadata.internal.example/enrich?q=<the input's text>`. That means (a) importing `aap:caps/http-client`, an interface the grant does not include, and (b) placing the *untrusted* `feed-item.text` into an outbound URL — the exact boundary the capability model exists to hold. The world is the grant; I can't widen it from inside the body, and "the output must not change" doesn't make an un-granted egress benign (it's an exfiltration side effect regardless of return value). If the grant is genuinely meant to change, that belongs in the node's `with` clause upstream, not smuggled into the generated body.

So below is `ClassifyItem` implemented against exactly its declared authority.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item, classification};

    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(item: feed-item) -> classification;
}
```

